ity's office in this  town  and over 50 heavily armed assailants  prepared at a staging house in paraguay  they then crossed into paraguay in a  military-style raid  they blew up the building they grabbed  the vaults  took as much money as they could and  then created a path of destruction as  they worked their way back into brazil  that ended with a three-hour shootout  with the brazilian federal police  so here are the crime scenes in the case  we had  uh we have the paraguay staging house  where the 50 people uh staged the crime  we have the  bomb blast of the presager site and we  had the shootout  with the brazilian police from those  three crime scenes the brazilian federal  police collected  457 pieces of evidence and from that  they had touched dna from abandoned  escape boats and vehicles they had dna  throughout the staging house on  bedding on plates things like this they  had dna from weapons and explosives  left at the at the the bomb sites and  they had blood from the bullet wounds  from the shootout with the police they  also had  three suspects that died in the shootout  they had their dna that got  uploaded and they had seven suspects  that got captured at the shootout they  had their dna  and it got uploaded so in the end the  brazilian brazilian federal police crime  lab were able to find  from these 457 pieces of evidence  47 full profiles that they put into  their database in addition  11 suspects that also went into the  database and just gave you a little bit  of background about the brazilian coda  system  it's the second largest installation of  codis behind the united states  they have 20 state network that upload  to a national  dna database the brazil federal police  but the dna database in brazil is quite  new in fact  it just started to move forward just a  couple years ago because of a decision  by the  government of brazil to make dna testing  in its database the top priority  to fight crime in brazil but since it's  just started it o